sequenceDiagram
    title UC1 · Place an Order · Thiha Aung (523K0073)
    actor Customer
    participant UI as Checkout page
    participant HTTP as Checkout routes
    participant Checkout as Checkout service
    participant DB as SQLite

    Customer->>UI: Choose hub and items
    UI->>HTTP: GET checkout catalog
    HTTP->>DB: Read hubs, areas and available menu items
    DB-->>UI: Catalog through checkout routes
    Customer->>UI: Enter address and optionally a voucher
    UI->>HTTP: POST quote
    HTTP->>Checkout: Resolve demo customer and calculate quote
    Checkout->>DB: Read distance, active load, item prices and voucher
    alt Hub unavailable or outside coverage
        Checkout->>DB: Find eligible alternatives for this cart
        Checkout-->>UI: Explain issue and show eligible hubs
    else Voucher invalid or input rejected
        Checkout-->>UI: Explain why checkout cannot proceed
    else Eligible quote
        Checkout-->>UI: Itemized price and total
    end

    Customer->>UI: Choose payment and place order
    UI->>HTTP: POST submit with checkout reference and expected total
    HTTP->>Checkout: Submit for resolved demo customer
    Checkout->>DB: Begin write transaction and find existing payment/order
    alt Order already submitted
        DB-->>Checkout: Stored receipt
        Checkout->>DB: Commit
        Checkout-->>UI: Return the existing receipt
    else New attempt or retry
        Checkout->>DB: Recheck eligibility and current total
        alt Quote changed or order is ineligible
            Checkout->>DB: Roll back
            Checkout-->>UI: Ask customer to review or revise the order
        else Quote accepted
            Checkout->>DB: Create or reuse payment in Pending state
            opt Online payment
                Checkout->>Checkout: Simulate payment approval or decline
                Checkout->>DB: Store authorization status and reference
            end
            alt Payment declined
                Checkout->>DB: Commit payment without order
                Checkout-->>UI: Show decline, retry and cancel choices
            else COD or approval
                Checkout->>DB: Insert Submitted order and item snapshots
                Checkout->>DB: Commit order and payment
                Checkout-->>UI: Show order ID, hub, total and status
            end
        end
    end

    opt Customer cancels before submission
        UI->>HTTP: POST cancel with checkout reference
        HTTP->>Checkout: Cancel for resolved demo customer
        Checkout->>DB: Archive existing unsubmitted payment, if present
        Checkout-->>UI: Show cancellation
    end
